ZVSE2

; Combat_BattleShadows (v10) example. Put this file into the Data\s folder of your mod. See README.md.
; Shadows are drawn by the game's own cursor shadow function, exactly like Fireball aiming. They need the game's
; "cursor shadow" combat option, like Fireball's area does.

; Example 1 (on): a radius 1 shadow that follows the mouse by itself, with blinking outlines.
;   P(radius)/(contour): radius 0..4 (0 = only the mouse hex), -1 = off; contour 1 = blinking blue outline.
;   It stays on until switched off or until the next battle action, so calling it on every hint is fine.
!?MM0;
!!FU(BattleShadow_Follow):P1/1;

; Example 2 (off): leave stacks out of the shadow. Here: every stack of side 1 (stacks 21..41).
; To turn it on, replace the first character * with ! on the next lines.
*?MM0;
*!re i/21/41;
*!BMi:N?y30;
*!co&y30<=0;
*!BMi:P?y32;
*!FU(BattleShadow_SkipStacks):Py32;
*!en;

; Example 3 (off): whole stacks, for chain spells. Two target stacks given by one of their hexes.
*?MM0;
*!FU(BattleShadow_Stacks):P52/120/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/-1/1;

; Example 5 (off): Frost Ring, a radius 1 ring without its centre hex, with outlines.
*?MM0;
*!MM:D?y9;
*!FU(BattleShadow_Radius):Py9/1/1;
*!FU(BattleShadow_SkipHexes):Py9;

; Example 4 (off): hide the movement range of the active stack while a spell is aimed, as Fireball aiming does.
;   P1 = hide (stays hidden until P0), P0 = show again, P1/1 = hide until the next battle action starts.
;   Calling it again with the same value does nothing, so it can be called in every hint.
;   P0 works the range out again from the stack's current speed: put a changed speed back before P0.
;   After a speed change while the range is shown: !!FU(BattleShadow_RefreshMovement):P;
;   Here ^My_Spell_Aiming^ stands for your own variable that is 1 while your mod aims a spell.
*?MM0;
*!SN:W^My_Spell_Aiming^/?y1;
*!FU(BattleShadow_HideMovement)&y1=0:P0;
*!FU(BattleShadow_HideMovement)&y1=1:P1;

; Diagnostics (off): shows the plugin state in the battle hint line instead of the normal hint.
*!FU(BattleShadow_Debug):P?y20/?y21/?y22/?y23/?y24/?y25/?y26/?y27/?y28/?y29/?y30/?y31/?y32;
*!MM:M^v%y20 shown=%y21 hint=%y22 follow=%y23 skip=%y24 game=%y25 own=%y26 full=%y27 cursor=%y28 opt=%y29 hook=%y30 move=%y31 xhex=%y32^;
